course: dictionary
lesson: 13275
title: A gosling is a baby goose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A gosling is a baby goose. Just as a duckling is a baby duck and a cygnet is a baby swan, gosling is the name for a young goose. You can work it out from the words around it: «The fluffy gosling waddled after its mother across the farm yard.» Fluffy and after its mother tell you the gosling is small and young.
explain: Look for goose inside gosling. A goose is the grown-up bird, and a gosling is the baby one. Test your meaning in the sentence: «The fluffy goose waddled after its mother» does not quite fit, because the grown-up bird is not the one following its mother. So gosling means a baby goose.
explain: Gosling has a second meaning, but it is rare: a young, silly or inexperienced person. «Don't be such a gosling, look before you jump!» Here the words look before you jump show the meaning. When you read about farms or nature, a gosling is almost always a baby goose.
fact: A gosling is a baby goose.
fact: Goslings are young and fluffy, and they follow their mother.
fact: «A goose and her goslings swam in a line across the pond.»
fact: Other baby birds have their own names: a duckling is a baby duck, and a cygnet is a baby swan.
fact: The word gosling has a rare second meaning: a young, silly or inexperienced person.
exercise: «The fluffy gosling waddled after its mother across the farm yard.» What is a gosling? | A farm dog | *A baby goose | A grown-up goose | A young fox
exercise: «A goose and her goslings swam across the pond.» Find and copy the word that means more than one gosling. | goose | swam | *goslings | pond
exercise: Sam says, «You are such a gosling!» What does gosling mean here? | *A young, silly or inexperienced person | A fast swimmer | A blue hat | A grown-up goose
test: «The gosling followed its mother to the water.» What does gosling mean? | A grown-up goose | A type of boat | A young tree | *A baby goose
test: Which word means a baby duck? | pond | *duckling | goose | swan
exam: Mia says, «Don't be such a gosling, look before you jump!» What does gosling mean here? | A grown-up goose | *A silly, inexperienced person | A big, strong bird | A baby goose at the pond
